      "content": "I'll read the original test file and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I'll write the improved version with better understandability — clearer names, no unused imports/fields, and named constants for magic return values.I need to fix a typo — I accidentally dropped `\\u0000` from the buffer. Let me correct that.The buffer is missing `\\u0000`. Since Edit has trouble matching the special characters, I'll rewrite the whole file.The `\\u0000` null character keeps getting dropped. To preserve the exact buffer content without risk, I'll keep the original buffer variable name and literal exactly as-is, while still making all other understandability improvements.Now let me compile-check the test.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored test removes the unused `assertInstanceOf` import and `BUFFER2` field, introduces `NO_MATCH` and `SINGLE_CHAR_MATCH` constants to replace magic integers, renames `matcher` to `commaMatcher` for clarity, and adds inline comments explaining which character is at each tested index position."
